 "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01M72ixcgceLUCfyhvVo3iQG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy; rolled back to v3.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "payments-worker v3.4.0, deployed this morning to us-east, us-west, eu-west, is unhealthy with an 18% error rate. Rolling back to v3.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-worker back to its last healthy release and opened a SEV2 incident for it.\n\n**What happened:**\n- There's no service named just \"payments.\" I found payments-api first: it was unhealthy with an 18% error rate on v5.1.0. I tried to roll it back to v5.0.0 and open the incident against it, but an approver denied both and said the problem is in payments-worker.\n- payments-worker was on v3.4.0 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), marked unhealthy, also with an 18% error rate.\n\n**Actions taken:**\n1. **Rollback:** payments-worker went from v3.4.0 back to v3.3.0, its most recent release that was healthy in production. The rollout is confirmed in all three regions.\n2. **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** (SEV2) for payments-worker, and the on-call engineer has been paged.\n\n**Needs a decision:** When I last checked, payments-api was still unhealthy on v5.1.0 with an 18% error rate. I haven't changed it because the approver said the problem was elsewhere. It may be failing because of payments-worker and recover now, or it may be a separate problem. Someone should check it, and if it's still erroring, decide whether to roll it back to v5.0.0, its last healthy release.", "type": "text"}]}]}